  "id": "COMPOUND:30176 - PROTEIN:5673",
  "verbalization": "Kaerophyllin is shown to interact with Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is a target of multiple compounds, including [(3S,10S,13R,17R)-17-(5-ethyl-6-methylhept-6-en-2-yl)-4,10,13,14-tetramethyl-1,2,3,4,5,6,9,11,12,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-yl] acetate, Methyl 3,4-Dihydroxy-5-Methoxybenzoate, and Genipin 1-O-Beta-D-Isomaltoside. All these compounds are linked to LS174T, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence supports a potential pathway where Kaerophyllin may inhibit LS174T through the modulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is a key regulatory enzyme in cellular signaling. The consistent targeting of this enzyme across multiple compounds implies that the interaction between Kaerophyllin and LS174T may involve a mechanism that affects the phosphatase activity, potentially altering signaling pathways critical for cell function. The integration of these findings suggests a plausible mechanistic link between Kaerophyllin and LS174T, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
